Now the banner shows RED nicely. The car has moved (speed 251 km/h), camera chase; the player car is not visible? It's out of frame at bottom? The camera seems too far forward/low? We see trail particles center and a red car (NOVA) at left, ball high near goal. The player car may be below frame because camera follows but maybe car is at bottom edge? Actually camera behind car; car should be centered lower. It's not visible. Why? At high speed, camera back distance increases (13.6 + speed*0.055; speed ~70 → 17.4) and camera height 8.0; car should still be in view lower center. Hmm the trail particles at center suggest player is there but invisible? Maybe the car is clipped by near plane or hidden behind HUD? Could be below frame. The camera look target is blended 60% toward ball, which may be high/forward, tilting view up and pushing car below frame. At speed, ball is near goal and high; look target lerps to ball; camera looks up, car falls below. This is a common ball-cam issue. Need keep car visible: clamp look target y relative to car, and blend less / adjust camera height. Use ball cam target but limit vertical: `look.y = Math.min(look.y, player.pos.y + 5)` and maybe raise camera. Also reduce blend to 0.45. Or place camera higher and further when looking at ball. Let's compute: camera pos y=6.6+speed*.02 ~8; look target ball y maybe 6? car y 0; camera looks at y 6 at z ball, so horizon; car below. The camera should look at a point lower, e.g. ball but with y clamp to 4.5, or blend look toward car more.

Rocket League ball cam keeps car in lower third. Set look target = player.pos + up*2.2 + forward*6; then if ballCam, lerp toward ball but cap the y at 4.5 and limit horizontal? Use:
```
if (ballCam) {
  const ballLook = ball.pos.clone();
  ballLook.y = clamp(ballLook.y, 1.2, 5.5);
  look.lerp(ballLook, 0.5);
}
```
Still car may be lower but visible. Also camera height 6.6; at distance 17, look at 5.5 => car bottom maybe. Reduce camera look-up. Let's set look y = player.pos.y + 2.2 + (ball.y - 2.2)*0.35, so ball height contributes less. For ball high 8, look y=2.2+2.0=4.2. Good.
```
if (ballCam) {
 const ballY = clamp(ball.pos.y, 1.5, 7);
 look.set(player.pos.x*0.4 + ball.pos.x*0.6, 2.2 + (ballY-2)*0.4, player.pos.z*0.4 + ball.pos.z*0.6);
}
```
But horizontal look at ball is fine. Keep car visible by raising camera to 7.5 and looking at ball low.

Also the car may be missing because the player's car is actually behind camera due to camera snap? Wait at kickoff cameraSnap true sets camera behind; after driving, camera follows. Player speed 251 km/h = 69.7 m/s, which is above max 36 m/s; 251 km/h from speed 69.7; how? Max speed 52 with boost = 52 m/s = 187 km/h. 251 means speed 69.7; perhaps car velocity includes lateral? Or car got hit by item/boost? Boost 16; speed 251 suggests it was hit by something or bug. Wait player speed = hypot(vel.x, vel.z); maxSpeed cap 52 with boost, but car could be launched by bomb/shell impulse (13) or collision. Or maybe input keydown W didn't register and something else? It drove straight; speed 251 after 2s with boost? Acceleration 38 + boost 64 = 102 m/s², cap 52; should cap at 52. But our clamp only applies vF damp toward cap when vF > cap; with dt 1/90, after 2s game time maybe 52. 251 km/h = 69.7. Hmm maybe because `this.speed` includes vertical? No, hypot(x,z). Could be the car was hit by a red shell or star, adding velocity 13; or the ball collision? Or "boostTime" from mushroom? No item. Maybe AI hit? Or car launched and landed? Hmm.

